    m_VerticalOverflow: 1
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Long ago, there was a forgotten forest called Elwyn.\n\nThe leaves here
    glow. The streams sing. Mushrooms start conversations \u2014 though mostly nonsense.
    Elwyn is not a dangerous place. It's more like a playful magic school: classrooms
    in tree hollows, textbooks on branches, and your teacher might be a talking flower
    by the roadside.\n\nNo one knows how old the forest is. Some say it was planted
    by the oldest mage with their last tear. Others say it is magic itself \u2014
    as long as you believe in kindness, it will appear.\n\nBut one thing is certain:
    many little fairies and talking animals live here, along with a legendary witch
    \u2014 Granny Meriel.\nShe is the guardian of the forest. Powerful in magic,
    but with the heart of an old child. She loves to laugh and play, and enjoys writing
    her spellbook in the Moonlit Glade. She poured everything she knew \u2014 courage,
    kindness, listening, mending \u2014 into a thick, heavy book.\n\nBut she left
    the book to no one. She said, \"Learning it all at once \u2014 where's the fun
    in that?\"\n\nSo one windy evening, she tore the book into five pages.\n\nAfter
    that, people would occasionally come looking for the pages. Some found two. Some
    found three. Some found nothing. But no one who ever gathered all five pages
    ever saw Granny Meriel again.\n\nYou are the next one to push open that door."
